From a8804318866231a27450c94ced50e2471e068c93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.taile7bcb.ts.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:28:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 55/60] dsv4 topk_v2: exact, deterministic top-k (ties by
 lowest index; no 2,048-candidate cap) (recipe T3.15d)

topk_impl.cuh breaks exact score ties by atomicAdd arrival order and keeps at most
kMaxNumTie (2,048) candidates of the threshold bin, so the selected SET of k
positions is run-dependent whenever the k-th score is tied (relu-style zero
scores already do it) and inexact when > 2,048 scores share one fp16 bin
(sgl-project/sglang #35257).

Both paths (register/streaming `refine_and_collect`, cluster `cluster_refine`)
now refine the threshold bin with a 64-bit key (exact_bin << 32 | ~idx), one
radix byte per round, so the result equals a stable sort by (value desc, idx asc):
  * `scan_threshold` picks the byte that straddles the remaining rank; rounds
    emit candidates above it and keep the equal ones; `RefineState` carries the
    (v_lo, v_hi) window plus the fixed prefix/mask;
  * constant-bit detection (per-thread AND/OR folded cluster-wide) skips bytes
    that cannot split the candidates, so a one-value tie over 262K positions
    needs 3 passes instead of 8;
  * the collect is merged into the last round's pass; a non-last round with
    nothing above the matched byte needs no pass;
  * `handle_tie` -> `radix_tie_select` ranks the survivors by (value, ~idx) in
    two exact passes instead of a value-only pass with arrival-order fill;
  * histogram adds are warp-aggregated when the active lanes share a bin
    (two shuffles; cheaper than __match_any_sync on divergent bins).

Verified offline (recipe evidence/t315d/offline/): against torch stable sort on
61 cases (zero ties, 2,049..60,000-way ties, >2,048 in one bin, ragged tails,
short rows, randn control; register, streaming and cluster paths) every result
is exact and stable; stock is wrong in every tied case. Tie-free rows cost the
same as stock (randn 262K: 40 vs 41 us). Degenerate rows cost more than stock's
(wrong) answer: zero-tie 262K 64 -> 199 us, 65K 25 -> 60 us.

